  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 11,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.137,
            0.046,
            0.346,
            0.063
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.088,
            0.469,
            0.107
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Consider the numbers 1, 8, 27, ..."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.107,
            0.848,
            0.143
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "These numbers are called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "perfect cubes.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Can you see why they are named so?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.143,
            0.848,
            0.181
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Each of them is obtained by multiplying a number by itself three times. We note that"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.439,
            0.186,
            0.559,
            0.205
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_11_equation_4.jpg",
          "content": "1 = 1 \\times 1 \\times 1"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.438,
            0.209,
            0.56,
            0.228
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_11_equation_5.jpg",
          "content": "8 = 2 \\times 2 \\times 2"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.434,
            0.233,
            0.565,
            0.253
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_11_equation_6.jpg",
          "content": "2 7 = 3 \\times 3 \\times 3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.26,
            0.272,
            0.284
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Is 9 a cube?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.286,
            0.738,
            0.326
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We see that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 \\times 2 \\times 2 = 8"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 \\times 3 \\times 3 = 2 7"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . This shows that 9 is not a perfect cube. Nor is any number from 10 to 26."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.746,
            0.204,
            0.941,
            0.345
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.746,
                0.204,
                0.941,
                0.345
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_11_image_9.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.334,
            0.736,
            0.374
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? Can you estimate the number of unit cubes in a cube with an edge length of 4 units?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.378,
            0.682,
            0.452
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "It has 64 unit cubes! If you notice carefully, each layer of this cube has "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 \\times 4"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " unit cubes. Each square layer has 16 unit cubes "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( 4 \\times 4 )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , and there are 4 such layers, so the total number of unit cubes is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 \\times 4 \\times 4 = 64."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.451,
            0.527,
            0.47
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "5^{3} = 5 \\times 5 \\times 5 = 125,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , 125 is a cube."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.47,
            0.681,
            0.508
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In general, for any number n, we write the cube",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\pmb { n } \\times \\pmb { n } \\times \\pmb { n }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n ^ { 3 } ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.686,
            0.361,
            0.942,
            0.544
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
